# External plan review — OpenRouter

Two reviewers completed. One approved; one requested revision. Incorporated findings:

- fail closed on malformed/unsafe state rather than treating it as empty;
- acquire owner lock before publishing a permanently unique ticket;
- normalize all weights to the hardware capacity so the FIFO head always fits;
- define a non-nested uv-then-CPU lifetime to avoid deadlock and idle CPU reservation;
- key sibling worktrees by resolved Git common directory and isolate separate clones;
- use a private per-user runtime root with link/object validation;
- make ticket-file cleanup bounded/best-effort, never part of correctness;
- require native Windows subprocess/crash evidence under the existing CI matrix;
- send queue and heartbeat diagnostics as single stderr lines.

Final disposition: revised plan accepted as build basis.
